    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required exposing an `initials` field on the owner API \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`). The acceptance test reads `$.initials` from `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nI followed the existing `displayName` computed-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), mirroring the existing `displayName` definition.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` passes (`\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`) and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures.",
